WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.125
Imagine a cafe starting with pen and paper

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.325
Then orders pile up What if its tools could

00:00:07.338 --> 00:00:08.212
grow with the work

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.762
Start with a request Make me a sales table

00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:17.512
for coffee and cake Tabletop drafts it Review

00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:19.625
it apply it and start using it

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:25.408
Now the shop gets busy Entering every sale

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.045
is too slow Add buttons so I can record a sale

00:00:29.058 --> 00:00:29.933
with one click

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:35.620
The buttons join the same canvas Click Coffee

00:00:35.783 --> 00:00:38.058
the count goes up and the total updates

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:43.467
Want to see what's selling Ask for a chart

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:47.017
Once approved it reads the same sales data

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.430
There's nothing to enter again

00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:54.921
Trying an afternoon offer Add and approve a

00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:58.320
ten-percent discount The rule calculates the

00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:00.096
net total from today's sales

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.788
Change your mind Select that rule and ask for

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.462
twenty percent Review the new result then apply

00:01:09.475 --> 00:01:13.400
it Your table buttons and chart stay in place

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.800
Tabletop Start small use it and shape it as

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:22.900
you go Tools that keep adapting to you
